From 9ebce4477ba6bac30eaf7b6cb9244cbf38a1cfd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:26:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): sync frontend tokenomics constants to RFC-006
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Frontend (contract.ts, types.ts, engine.ts) still implemented the
pre-RFC-006 model: 200 KVNC subsidy, binary halving every 500,000
blocks, no supply cap. The node and TESTNET-RFC006.md have shipped
the real model for a while: 10 KVNC genesis subsidy, geometric decay
(alpha=3/4) every 2,000,000 blocks, 90.2M KVNC hard cap. Docs page
and generated /api/spec text were showing the stale numbers to users.

- contract.ts: SUBSIDY 200->10 KVNC, added ERA_LENGTH (2M, replaces
  HALVING_ERA as the canonical name; HALVING_ERA kept as a deprecated
  alias so existing call sites don't need to change in this same
  commit), added MAX_SUPPLY (90.2M) and DECAY_ALPHA_NUM/DEN (3/4).
  Also fixed FOUNDER_AMOUNT: was 200 KVNC, should be 200,000 KVNC
  (0.2M founder premine per RFC-006) — a separate, previously-missed
  bug (3 zeros short), caught while auditing every constant against
  the doc instead of just the one everyone was looking at.
- types.ts: removed its own independent SUBSIDY/ATOM/K definitions
  (a second, drifted source of truth) in favor of re-exporting the
  same values from contract.ts, so the two can't diverge again.
- engine.ts subsidyAt(): replaced `subsidy / 2^era` (binary halving)
  with the actual RFC-006 geometric decay (`s = floor(s*3/4)` per
  era, capped at 256 eras same as the node) — this was a different
  formula, not just a wrong number.
- spec.ts / docs.tsx: "Premine" was reading SUBSIDY (block reward)
  instead of FOUNDER_AMOUNT + TREASURY_AMOUNT (actual premine) —
  wrong field, independent of the value bug. Added Max supply as a
  visible fact on both. Verified subsidyAt(0/2M/4M) against hand
  calculation (10 / 7.5 / 5.625 KVNC) and confirmed generated
  /api/spec text now matches TESTNET-RFC006.md verbatim.

Scope note: ApiHead/ApiBootstrap types and the local mock node still
don't expose native_minted/circulating/burned/max_supply fields from
the live node's /api/head response — no UI currently reads them, so
that's a separate follow-up, not folded into this fix.

Verified with tsc --noEmit and eslint (0 errors/warnings on touched
files).
